## 2. Streaming Output via SSE

Both implementations use **Server-Sent Events (SSE)** to stream responses to the browser.

### Python

The endpoint returns a FastAPI `StreamingResponse`:

```python
# _endpoint.py, lines 139-147
return StreamingResponse(
    event_generator(),
    media_type="text/event-stream",
    headers={
        "Cache-Control": "no-cache",
        "Connection": "keep-alive",
        "X-Accel-Buffering": "no",
    },
)
```

The `event_generator()` iterates over events from `protocol_runner.run(input_data)`, encodes each as JSON via `EventEncoder.encode(event)`, and yields the `data: <json>` line.

### .NET

The `AGUIServerSentEventsResult` uses `System.Net.ServerSentEvents.SseFormatter`:

```csharp
// AGUIServerSentEventsResult.cs, lines 45-49
await SseFormatter.WriteAsync(
    WrapEventsAsSseItemsAsync(this._events, cancellationToken),
    body,
    this.SerializeEvent,
    cancellationToken);
```

The `SerializeEvent` method writes each event as JSON:

```csharp
// Lines 97-108
private void SerializeEvent(SseItem<BaseEvent> item, IBufferWriter<byte> writer)
{
    if (this._jsonWriter == null)
        this._jsonWriter = new Utf8JsonWriter(writer);
    else
        this._jsonWriter.Reset(writer);
    JsonSerializer.Serialize(this._jsonWriter, item.Data, AGUIJsonSerializerContext.Default.BaseEvent);
}
```

### Event Types in the Stream

The server emits a sequence of typed AG-UI events:

| Event | Purpose |
|-------|---------|
| `RUN_STARTED` | Marks the beginning of a run; includes `threadId` and `runId` |
| `TEXT_MESSAGE_START` | Opens a text message block with a `messageId` |
| `TEXT_MESSAGE_CONTENT` | Delta text chunk (streaming) |
| `TEXT_MESSAGE_END` | Closes the text message block |
| `TOOL_CALL_START` | LLM wants to call a tool; includes `toolCallId` and `toolCallName` |
| `TOOL_CALL_ARGS` | Delta arguments for the tool call |
| `TOOL_CALL_END` | Tool call arguments complete |
| `TOOL_CALL_RESULT` | Result of a tool execution |
| `STATE_SNAPSHOT` | Shared state update for the UI |
| `RUN_FINISHED` | Run complete; may include `interrupt` metadata for human-in-the-loop |
| `RUN_ERROR` | Error occurred during streaming |

